#X text 30 20 CLOCK CONTENTION TEST -- does u_tempo's 24 PPQN starve note-outs to the 404 at high tempo. BOTH variables are driven from the Mac so nobody has to turn two knobs and listen at the same time., f 100;
#X text 330 300 THE QUESTION. u_tempo sends 24 PPQN to TWO ports -- the Launchpad and the 404. At the 600 BPM clamp that is 240 pulses per second each \, so 480 messages per second in total \, which is ABOVE the 360-400 trigger ceiling measured in item 208., f 58;
#X text 330 420 BUT THE TEST MIGHT SHOW NOTHING \, and that would be the good outcome. A clock tick is ONE byte where a note on plus note off is SIX \, so if the transport is limited by BYTE rate rather than message rate the clock has roughly tenfold headroom and cannot starve anything. These two possibilities are what the test separates., f 58;
#X text 30 610 ⚠️ SEND tempo BEFORE rate. Writing the tempo bus closes u_map's seed spigot \, and doing it while triggers are already running makes the change harder to hear against a stream that is already dense., f 100;
#X connect 0 0 1 0;
#X connect 1 0 2 1;
